From: atty303 <atty303@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 16:20:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] rtworkq: release finalized serial queue items

serial_queue_submit() adds a reference while an item is on the serial queue's
pending list, and pool_queue_submit() adds another reference to keep the item
alive for its finalization callback. The worker releases the dispatch reference
when Invoke() returns.

The serial finalizer removes the completed item from the pending list but only
releases one reference. Release both the pending-list and finalizer references
after removing the item. Otherwise the leaked async result retains its callback
and can keep a Source Reader and its private queue handle alive indefinitely.

Also store the published generation-bearing user queue handle in queue->id, so
serial reply callbacks report the correct queue ID.

diff --git a/dlls/rtworkq/queue.c b/dlls/rtworkq/queue.c
--- a/dlls/rtworkq/queue.c
+++ b/dlls/rtworkq/queue.c
@@ -461,6 +461,8 @@ static void CALLBACK serial_queue_finalization_callback(PTP_CALLBACK_INSTANCE instance, void *user_data)
 
     LeaveCriticalSection(&queue->cs);
 
+    /* Release both the pending-list reference and the reference held for this finalizer. */
+    IUnknown_Release(&item->IUnknown_iface);
     IUnknown_Release(&item->IUnknown_iface);
 }
 
@@ -1008,6 +1010,7 @@ static HRESULT alloc_user_queue(const struct queue_desc *desc, DWORD *queue_id)
     entry->generation = queue_generation;
     idx = entry - user_queues + FIRST_USER_QUEUE_HANDLE;
     *queue_id = (idx << 16) | entry->generation;
+    queue->id = *queue_id;
 
     LeaveCriticalSection(&queues_section);
 
